Haan bhai, ye “SDK not found” wala error 90% cases me environment issue hota hai — code ka masla nahi hota 👍
Tumne build dusre PC pe ki, isliye wahan Android SDK properly set nahi hoga.

Chalo simple language me reasons + solution dono dekhte hain:

🔴 Common Reasons (dusre PC par)
Android SDK install hi nahi

Android Studio install nahi

Ya SDK download nahi hua

ANDROID_HOME / ANDROID_SDK_ROOT set nahi

System ko pata hi nahi ke SDK kahan rakha hua hai

Gradle ko SDK ka path nahi mil raha

local.properties missing ya galat

JDK version mismatch

Java install nahi ya wrong version (RN ke liye Java 17 best hai)

✅ Step by Step Solution
✅ 1. Check Android SDK installed hai ya nahi
Dusre PC pe Android Studio open karo

Settings → Appearance & Behavior → System Settings → Android SDK

Path note karo, usually hota hai:

C:\Users\USERNAME\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk
✅ 2. Environment Variable set karo
Windows me:

This PC → Properties → Advanced system settings → Environment Variables

Add karo:

System Variables:

ANDROID_HOME = C:\Users\USERNAME\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk
Aur PATH me add karo:

%ANDROID_HOME%\platform-tools
%ANDROID_HOME%\tools
%ANDROID_HOME%\tools\bin
PC restart karo ✔️

✅ 3. local.properties file check karo
Path:

android/local.properties
Isme ye hona chahiye:

sdk.dir=C:\\Users\\USERNAME\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
⚠️ Single \ mat use karna, double \\ use karo

✅ 4. Java version check karo
CMD me:

java -version
RN ke liye best:

Java 17
Agar Java nahi:
👉 install OpenJDK 17

✅ 5. Clean build karo
cd android
gradlew clean
cd ..
npx react-native run-android
Ya agar sirf build:

cd android
gradlew assembleDebug
